---
import Figure from '../Figure.astro';
---

<Figure
  caption="POMC, PCSK1 or LEPR deficiency or hypothalamic injury can reduce melanocortin input to MC4R. Setmelanotide activates MC4R downstream of that impaired input."
  source="Mechanism: StatPearls NBK589641 · The leptin–melanocortin pathway"
>
  <svg class="schematic" viewBox="0 0 400 310" role="img" aria-label="Setmelanotide bypasses impaired signaling upstream of MC4R">
    <desc>Impaired leptin–POMC signaling can reduce α-MSH input to MC4R. Setmelanotide directly activates MC4R, which helps regulate satiety and energy expenditure.</desc>
    <rect class="node" x="16" y="20" width="176" height="72" rx="6" />
    <text x="104" y="47">Leptin → POMC</text>
    <text class="detail" x="104" y="73">α-MSH production</text>
    <rect class="active-node" x="208" y="20" width="176" height="72" rx="6" />
    <text x="296" y="47">Setmelanotide</text>
    <text class="detail" x="296" y="73">MC4R agonist</text>

    <path class="flow blocked-flow" d="M104 92 V113 M104 148 V171 H155" />
    <text class="detail" x="104" y="136">Reduced input</text>
    <path class="flow muted-flow" d="M156 165 V177" />
    <path class="flow" d="M296 92 V171 H244 m5-5-5 5 5 5" />

    <rect class="active-node" x="166" y="150" width="68" height="42" rx="6" />
    <text x="200" y="177">MC4R</text>
    <path class="flow" d="M200 192 V227 m-5-5 5 5 5-5" />
    <rect class="node" x="40" y="236" width="320" height="52" rx="6" />
    <text x="200" y="268">Satiety and energy expenditure</text>
  </svg>
</Figure>
